CERT: DCL00-J
For use case:

class A {
  public static final int a = B.b + 1;
  // ...
}

class B {
  public static final int b = A.a + 1;
  // ...
}

CERT: DCL00-J
For use case:

public class Cycle {
  private final int balance;
  private static final Cycle c = new Cycle();
  private static final int deposit = (int) (Math.random() * 100); // Random deposit

  public Cycle() {
    balance = deposit - 10; // Subtract processing fee
  }

  public static void main(String[] args) {
    System.out.println("The account balance is: " + c.balance);
  }
}

StructuralRule.Predicate:
FunctionCall fc: function is [Function: constructor and isBodyAvailable
        /* and isn't the default constructor (automatically generated by SCA) */
        and not sourceLocation.null
        and not enclosingClass.sourceLocation.null
        and sourceLocation.startLine != enclosingClass.sourceLocation.startLine
        /* calling constructor of own class */
        and enclosingClass == fc.enclosingClass
        /* constructor contains static FieldAccess initialized after original assignmentStatement */
        and contains
            [FieldAccess fa: field is
                [Field field: static
                    and field.enclosingClass == fc.enclosingClass
                    and not sourceLocation.null
                    and not fc.sourceLocation.null
                    and sourceLocation.startLine > fc.sourceLocation.startLine
                    /* would like to say field was not initialize to constant value, but can't find a way to do this */
                    and labels contains [String s: s == "UninitializedStaticField"]
                ]*
                and not enclosingStatement is [AssignmentStatement: lhs === fa]
            ]*
        ]*
    and enclosingFunction is [Function f: name == "<static>"]

